+# macOS 10.15 (Catalina)
+
+Not an official target: the README says macOS 12. This page is what was checked and what it takes.
+
+## What you need
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Xcode | 12.4 (the last that runs on Catalina). The launcher needs the full Xcode, for `xcrun metal`. The game needs only its Command Line Tools |
+| Rust | 1.95 or newer (`rust-version` in `Cargo.toml`) |
+| JDK | Temurin **25.0.2**. Homebrew lists it as macOS 10.15+; later 25.0.x builds list macOS 11. Keep 25.0.2 |
+| GPU | One that supports Metal 2 (any Mac that runs Catalina has one, but older Intel iGPUs have fewer limits) |
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+tools/catalina/build.sh               # the game: horizon-client, horizon-ctl, horizon-prepare
+tools/catalina/build.sh --launcher    # and the launcher (needs full Xcode)
+tools/catalina/check.sh               # minimum OS, frameworks, `--help`; prints the smoke test
+```
+
+`build.sh` sets `MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=10.15`, so every C dependency targets 10.15 too. Then follow
+"Build from source" in the README (`horizon-prepare`, then `horizon-client`).
+
+## What was checked, and how
+
+Checked against the macOS 10.15 SDK's export lists (`.tbd` stubs), on the nightly 2026-11-07 Intel builds:
+
+| Program | Minimum macOS it declares | Symbols it binds that 10.15 lacks |
+|---|---|---|
+| `horizon-client`, `horizon-ctl`, `horizon-server`, `horizon-prepare` | 10.12 | none (466 / 113 / 176 / 134 bound) |
+| `horizon-launcher` 0.2.50 | 10.12 | `_UTTypeData`, `_UTTypeFolder`, and a hard link to `UniformTypeIdentifiers.framework` |
+
+So the game's programs should load on Catalina as shipped. **Not checked**: that they run well there (Metal
+limits on the GPU, performance); nothing was run on a Catalina Mac.
+
+## What the launcher patch changes
+
+The launcher's toolkit (GPUI) needs macOS 11 in three places. `launcher/Cargo.toml` patches them with copies
+in `third_party/`, each marked `Horizon:`:
+
+- `objc2-uniform-type-identifiers`: no `#[link]` to `UniformTypeIdentifiers.framework`.
+- `gpui-fast-macos`, `window.rs`: drag icons use `iconForFileType:` (10.0+), not `UTType` and
+  `iconForContentType:` (11+).
+- `gpui-fast-apple`, `build.rs`: Metal shaders are compiled for 10.15, not 12.0 (`HORIZON_METAL_MIN_MACOS`
+  sets it). The shaders use nothing newer than MSL 2.0.
+
+`Info.plist` says `LSMinimumSystemVersion` 10.15 instead of 12.0. Drop all of it when GPUI supports Catalina.
+The patched `gpui-fast-macos` type-checks for `x86_64-apple-darwin`; the launcher as a whole has not been built or run.
